JPMC Dining Data Modernization
Architecture Explained as Interview Questions
Q1. Tell me about your last project architecture.
Answer

In my last project at JPMC, I worked on a Dining Data Modernization platform.

The objective was to collect restaurant and lifestyle content from external providers, process and standardize the data, store it in AWS S3, and make it available for analytics and downstream business systems.

The platform was built using:

Spring Boot
Spring Batch
AWS S3
Kafka
AWS Glue
Athena
Aurora PostgreSQL
AWS ECS


The architecture followed an event-driven microservices design that provided:

Loose Coupling
Scalability
Fault Isolation
Independent Deployments
Cloud-Native Processing

