Final JPMC Manager/Architect Round Question
Q21. Summarize your project in one minute.
Answer

"I worked on JPMC's Dining Data Modernization platform where external dining content 
was ingested through Spring Batch extraction services, stored in AWS S3 for durability,
processed by publisher services, distributed through Kafka topics, consumed by analytics,
audit and notification services, transformed through AWS Glue, and reported through Athena. 
The solution was cloud-native, event-driven, highly scalable, fault-tolerant, and 
capable of processing large datasets using Spring Boot, Kafka, AWS ECS, Aurora PostgreSQL, S3, Glue, and Athena."
